//! Minimum circuits for every Boolean function of up to three inputs, one
//! table per instruction set: `WITH_EQ` may use `Eq`, `WITHOUT_EQ` (for
//! `functional-bool-v1`) may not.
//!
//! Generated by `cuts::generator`, a breadth-first search over sets of
//! computed functions; the test `cut_tables_are_their_generators_output`
//! regenerates both tables and compares, and
//! `every_cut_table_entry_computes_its_function` evaluates every entry. Do not
//! edit by hand.
//!
//! Entry `offset(vars) + f` is the circuit for function `f` of `vars` inputs,
//! with offsets 0, 2, 6 and 22 for 0, 1, 2 and 3 inputs; bit `t` of `f` is the
//! value when input `i` has value `t >> i & 1`. A circuit is a sequence of
//! gates separated by spaces: `T` and `F` (constants), `Na`, `Aab`, `Eab` and
//! `Scab` (Not, And, Eq, Select) whose digits name earlier operands (inputs
//! first, then gates in order). The last gate is the output; `@i` alone means
//! the output is input `i`. Inputs are free; every gate, constants included,
//! costs one instruction.

